#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:225
msgid "If you've set any environmental settings, please re-apply them now."
msgstr ""
"Pokud jste nastavili nějaké proměnné prostředí, nastavte je nyní znovu."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:225
msgid ""
"If not already done, [install Elasticsearch](/en/tutorials/install-"
"elasticsearch) now."
msgstr ""
"Pokud jste to ještě neudělali, nyní [nainstalujte Elasticsearch](/cs/"
"tutorials/install-elasticsearch)."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:225
msgid ""
"[Connect Elasticsearch with Zammad and rebuild its search index](/en/"
"tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch). The rebuild can safely run during "
"your work, but will cause a degraded search performance and may lead to "
"temporarily not found data."
msgstr ""
"[Propojte Elasticsearch se Zammadem a znovu sestavte jeho vyhledávací index]"
"(/cs/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch). Sestavování může bezpečně "
"probíhat během vaší práce, ale vyhledávání bude pomalejší a některá data "
"nemusí být dočasně nalezena."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:226
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting backup & restore"
msgstr "Řešení potíží se zálohováním a obnovou"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:232
msgid ""
"You can find some common problems below. If your issue is not listed, feel "
"free to consult the [Zammad Community](https://community.zammad.org/c/"
"trouble-running-zammad-this-is-your-place/5){target=_blank} for technical "
"assistance."
msgstr ""
"Níže najdete několik častých problémů. Pokud váš problém v seznamu není, "
"obraťte se s žádostí o technickou pomoc na [komunitu Zammadu](https://"
"community.zammad.org/c/trouble-running-zammad-this-is-your-place/5)"
"{target=_blank}."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exit codes"
msgstr "Návratové kódy"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:237
msgid ""
"Our backup & restore scripts come with exit codes to help you finding a "
"solution. However, we do not guarantee a complete error handling."
msgstr ""
"Naše skripty pro zálohování a obnovu vracejí návratové kódy, které vám "
"pomohou najít řešení. Úplné ošetření chyb však nezaručujeme."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:240
msgid ""
"Beside the exit codes, there are also error messages returned to standard "
"out."
msgstr ""
"Kromě návratových kódů se na standardní výstup vypisují i chybové zprávy."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:247
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code | Description / Situation                                                                                                                                                                |\n"
"|------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| `0`  | The script finished successfully (or the error is not handled).                                                                                                                        |\n"
"| `1`  | This is a general error. Most often used for script aborts due to incorrect information provided or information missing.                                                               |\n"
"| `2`  | There was an error with database handling. This usually either happens if your database server does not meet script requirements, login data being invalid or \"broken‟ database dumps. |\n"
"| `3`  | There were issues with file / folder permissions.                                                                                                                                      |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Kód | Popis / situace |\n"
"|------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| `0`  | Skript skončil úspěšně (nebo chyba není ošetřena). |\n"
"| `1`  | Obecná chyba. Nejčastěji se používá při přerušení skriptu kvůli nesprávně zadaným nebo chybějícím informacím. |\n"
"| `2`  | Došlo k chybě při práci s databází. Obvykle k tomu dochází, když databázový server nesplňuje požadavky skriptu, přihlašovací údaje jsou neplatné nebo jsou výpisy databáze \"poškozené\". |\n"
"| `3`  | Vyskytly se problémy s oprávněními souborů / složek. |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:248
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common problems"
msgstr "Časté problémy"

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Password authentication failed / peer authentication failed"
msgstr "Password authentication failed / peer authentication failed"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:255
msgid ""
"This indicates that the password of your Zammad DB user is either different "
"from your `database.yml` or the wrong database server may be contacted."
msgstr ""
"To znamená, že heslo databázového uživatele Zammadu se liší od hesla ve "
"vašem `database.yml`, nebo se kontaktuje nesprávný databázový server."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:258
msgid ""
"If your Zammad instance is running, it can be caused by falling back to "
"socket connection which is why you didn't notice."
msgstr ""
"Pokud vaše instance Zammadu běží, může to být způsobeno přechodem na "
"připojení přes socket, a proto jste si toho nevšimli."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:260
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "**What to do?**\n"
msgstr "**Co dělat?**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:264
msgid ""
"Ensure that the provided user credentials are correct. You can also consider "
"to use the `reset_db_password` script, you can find in the backup directory."
msgstr ""
"Ověřte, že zadané přihlašovací údaje jsou správné. Můžete také zvážit "
"použití skriptu `reset_db_password`, který najdete v adresáři záloh."

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ident authentication failed for user"
msgstr "Ident authentication failed for user"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:269
msgid ""
"This indicates your database server does require `ident` authentication.  "
"That authentication method is not supported by our scripts."
msgstr ""
"To znamená, že váš databázový server vyžaduje ověřování `ident`. Tuto metodu "
"ověřování naše skripty nepodporují."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:274
msgid ""
"Check the `pg_hba.conf` of your PostgreSQL-Server and adjust it if needed."
msgstr ""
"Zkontrolujte soubor `pg_hba.conf` vašeho PostgreSQL serveru a v případě "
"potřeby ho upravte."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:276
msgid "Usually, authentication can be allowed like this:"
msgstr "Ověřování lze obvykle povolit takto:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:277
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# THIS IS A SAMPLE AND MAY NOT FIT YOUR ENVIRONMENT\n"
"host    all             all             127.0.0.1/32            md5\n"
"host    all             all             ::1/128                 md5\n"
msgstr ""
"# THIS IS A SAMPLE AND MAY NOT FIT YOUR ENVIRONMENT\n"
"host    all             all             127.0.0.1/32            md5\n"
"host    all             all             ::1/128                 md5\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:286
msgid ""
"Please consult the official [PostgreSQL documentation](https://"
"www.postgresql.org/docs/){target=_blank} for this, as this is out of our "
"documentation scope."
msgstr ""
"Nahlédněte prosím do oficiální [dokumentace PostgreSQL](https://"
"www.postgresql.org/docs/){target=_blank}, protože to přesahuje rámec naší "
"dokumentace."

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:287
#, no-wrap
msgid "WARNING: You don't seem to have any attachments in the file system"
msgstr "WARNING: You don't seem to have any attachments in the file system"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:291
msgid ""
"This indicate that your instance currently does not save attachments to file "
"system."
msgstr ""
"To znamená, že vaše instance v současnosti neukládá přílohy do souborového "
"systému."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:294
msgid ""
"This warning will be shown once before creating an empty directory to allow "
"the backup process to continue successfully."
msgstr ""
"Toto varování se zobrazí jednou před vytvořením prázdného adresáře, aby "
"zálohování mohlo úspěšně pokračovat."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:298
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check and adjust your\n"
"[storage settings via console](/en/reference/rails-commands#storage-provider-setting)\n"
"or in Zammad's admin interface under _Settings > System > Storage_.\n"
msgstr ""
"Zkontrolujte a upravte\n"
"[nastavení úložiště přes konzoli](/cs/reference/rails-commands#nastaveni-zpusobu-ukladani)\n"
"nebo v administraci Zammadu v _Nastavení > Systém > Úložiště_.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "Helper script"
msgstr "Pomocný skript"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:301
#, no-wrap
msgid "Warning"
msgstr "Upozornění"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:305
msgid ""
"A script can potentially be destructive! You should **never** run scripts "
"which scopes you don't understand."
msgstr ""
"Skript může být potenciálně destruktivní! **Nikdy** nespouštějte skripty, "
"jejichž rozsahu nerozumíte."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:307
msgid "Be aware that you are running these scripts at your own risk."
msgstr "Mějte na paměti, že tyto skripty spouštíte na vlastní riziko."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:308
#, no-wrap
msgid "Database helper: (Re)set password"
msgstr "Pomocník pro databázi: (znovu)nastavení hesla"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:316
msgid "This script is working for PostgreSQL installations only."
msgstr "Tento skript funguje jen v instalacích s PostgreSQL."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:316
msgid "Only local database servers are supported (script changes user)."
msgstr ""
"Podporovány jsou jen lokální databázové servery (skript mění uživatele)."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:316
msgid "This script requires to be run as `root` or similar privileged user."
msgstr ""
"Tento skript je nutné spustit jako `root` nebo podobně privilegovaný "
"uživatel."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:316
msgid "Be aware that the script will automatically stop and start Zammad!"
msgstr "Skript automaticky zastaví a znovu spustí Zammad!"

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:317
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scopes"
msgstr "Rozsah použití"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:323
msgid ""
"The scope of this script are mostly package installations and especially "
"CentOS and SUSE operating systems. It might work on source code / "
"development installations as well, but this highly depends on your setup and "
"is out of scope."
msgstr ""
"Skript je určen hlavně pro balíčkové instalace, zejména na operačních "
"systémech CentOS a SUSE. Může fungovat i v instalacích ze zdrojového kódu / "
"vývojových instalacích, ale to velmi záleží na vašem nastavení a je mimo "
"rozsah."

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:324
#, no-wrap
msgid "Functionality"
msgstr "Funkce"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:329
msgid ""
"The script will do the following actions automatically for you, depending on "
"the situation. It will ask for your confirmation before performing actions."
msgstr ""
"Skript za vás podle situace automaticky provede následující akce. Před "
"provedením akcí si vyžádá vaše potvrzení."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:335
msgid ""
"If `database.yml` contains an empty password line, a new password will be "
"generated and set for the database user of Zammad. It will also be saved to "
"the configuration file."
msgstr ""
"Pokud `database.yml` obsahuje prázdný řádek s heslem, vygeneruje se nové "
"heslo a nastaví se databázovému uživateli Zammadu. Uloží se také do "
"konfiguračního souboru."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:335
msgid ""
"If `database.yml` contains a password, it will be used to set the password "
"of the Zammad database user."
msgstr ""
"Pokud `database.yml` obsahuje heslo, použije se k nastavení hesla "
"databázového uživatele Zammadu."

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:336
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "Použití"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:340
msgid ""
"Run the script with the command below and follow the instructions. No "
"specific configuration is required."
msgstr ""
"Spusťte skript příkazem níže a postupujte podle pokynů. Žádná zvláštní "
"konfigurace není potřeba."

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:341
#, no-wrap
msgid "/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_db_user_helper.sh\n"
msgstr "/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_db_user_helper.sh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:346
msgid ""
"If errors occur, the script will try to bring Zammad back online before "
"exiting."
msgstr ""
"Pokud dojde k chybám, skript se před ukončením pokusí Zammad znovu "
"zprovoznit."

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connect and configure Elasticsearch"
msgstr "Propojení a konfigurace Elasticsearch"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:11
msgid "This guide shows you how to connect Zammad with Elasticsearch."
msgstr "Tento návod ukazuje, jak propojit Zammad s Elasticsearch."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connect Elasticsearch with Zammad"
msgstr "Propojení Elasticsearch se Zammadem"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the Elasticsearch URL"
msgstr "Nastavení URL Elasticsearch"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:17
msgid "Set the Elasticsearch server address; adapt it to your scenario."
msgstr "Nastavte adresu serveru Elasticsearch; upravte ji podle svého scénáře."

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_url', 'https://localhost:9200')\"\n"
msgstr "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_url', 'https://localhost:9200')\"\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the Elasticsearch user and password"
msgstr "Nastavení uživatele a hesla Elasticsearch"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_user', 'elastic')\"\n"
msgstr "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_user', 'elastic')\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Replace `<password>` with the one you got during the installation of Elasticsearch. In case you need to create a new\n"
"password, run `/usr/share/elasticsearch/bin/elasticsearch-reset-password -u elastic`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nahraďte `<password>` heslem, které jste získali při instalaci Elasticsearch. Pokud potřebujete vytvořit nové\n"
"heslo, spusťte `/usr/share/elasticsearch/bin/elasticsearch-reset-password -u elastic`.\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_password', '<password>')\"\n"
msgstr "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_password', '<password>')\"\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add certificate to Zammad"
msgstr "Přidání certifikátu do Zammadu"

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add it via Rails console"
msgstr "Přidání přes konzoli Rails"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:41
msgid ""
"In case you are installing a new Zammad and didn't run through the getting "
"started wizard already, add the certificate via console:"
msgstr ""
"Pokud instalujete nový Zammad a ještě jste neprošli průvodcem úvodním "
"nastavením, přidejte certifikát přes konzoli:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo cat /etc/elasticsearch/certs/http_ca.crt | zammad run rails r \"SSLCertificate.create!(certificate: STDIN.read)\"\n"
msgstr "sudo cat /etc/elasticsearch/certs/http_ca.crt | zammad run rails r \"SSLCertificate.create!(certificate: STDIN.read)\"\n"

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add it via UI"
msgstr "Přidání přes uživatelské rozhraní"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In case you already have a running and configured Zammad, you can add the certificate in Zammad's admin settings\n"
"(_Settings > Security > SSL Certificates_) as an alternative. To show and copy the auto-generated certificate from\n"
"Elasticsearch, run:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pokud už máte spuštěný a nakonfigurovaný Zammad, můžete certifikát alternativně přidat v administraci Zammadu\n"
"(_Nastavení > Zabezpečení > SSL certifikáty_). Automaticky vygenerovaný certifikát Elasticsearch zobrazíte\n"
"a zkopírujete spuštěním:\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo cat /etc/elasticsearch/certs/http_ca.crt\n"
msgstr "sudo cat /etc/elasticsearch/certs/http_ca.crt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:58
msgid ""
"To add it in Zammad, either upload the certificate file or paste the content "
"in the dialog. Make sure to copy/paste the delimiters (e.g. `-----BEGIN "
"CERTIFICATE-----`) too."
msgstr ""
"Chcete-li ho přidat do Zammadu, buď nahrajte soubor certifikátu, nebo vložte "
"jeho obsah do dialogu. Nezapomeňte zkopírovat a vložit i oddělovače (např. "
"`-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----`)."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build/rebuild the searchindex"
msgstr "Sestavení / opětovné sestavení vyhledávacího indexu"

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optional settings"
msgstr "Volitelná nastavení"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:78
msgid ""
"We collected some useful settings you may want to apply. For further "
"information please have a look at [Elastic's documentation](https://"
"www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html)"
"{target=_blank}."
msgstr ""
"Shromáždili jsme několik užitečných nastavení, která můžete chtít použít. "
"Další informace najdete v [dokumentaci Elastic](https://www.elastic.co/guide/"
"en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html){target=_blank}."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "Index namespacing"
msgstr "Jmenné prostory indexů"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:83
msgid ""
"Useful when connecting multiple services or Zammad instances to a single "
"Elasticsearch server (to prevent name collisions during indexing)."
msgstr ""
"Užitečné při připojování více služeb nebo instancí Zammadu k jednomu serveru "
"Elasticsearch (aby nedocházelo ke kolizím názvů při indexování)."

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_index', Socket.gethostname.downcase + '_zammad')\"\n"
msgstr "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_index', Socket.gethostname.downcase + '_zammad')\"\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "File-attachment indexing rules"
msgstr "Pravidla indexování příloh"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:93
msgid ""
"Zammad supports searching in file attachments, which means Elasticsearch has "
"to index those, too. Limiting such indexing can help preserve system "
"resources."
msgstr ""
"Zammad podporuje vyhledávání v přílohách, což znamená, že je Elasticsearch "
"musí také indexovat. Omezení takového indexování může pomoci šetřit "
"systémové prostředky."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:95
msgid "Files with these extensions will not be indexed:"
msgstr "Soubory s těmito příponami se nebudou indexovat:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_ignore',\\\n"
"[ '.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg', '.mpeg', '.mpg', '.mov', '.bin', '.exe', '.box', '.mbox' ] )\"\n"
msgstr ""
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_ignore',\\\n"
"[ '.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg', '.mpeg', '.mpg', '.mov', '.bin', '.exe', '.box', '.mbox' ] )\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:102
msgid "Files larger than this size (in MB) will not be indexed:"
msgstr "Soubory větší než tato velikost (v MB) se nebudou indexovat:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_max_size_in_mb', 50)\"\n"
msgstr "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_max_size_in_mb', 50)\"\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "Asciifold"
msgstr "Asciifold"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:112
msgid ""
"By default, the [Asciifold feature of Elasticsearch](https://www.elastic.co/"
"docs/reference/text-analysis/analysis-asciifolding-tokenfilter)"
"{target=_blank} is enabled. This can be useful if you deal with text which "
"includes diacritics and/or umlauts."
msgstr ""
"Ve výchozím nastavení je [funkce Asciifold v Elasticsearch](https://"
"www.elastic.co/docs/reference/text-analysis/analysis-asciifolding-"
"tokenfilter){target=_blank} zapnutá. To se může hodit, pokud pracujete s "
"textem obsahujícím diakritiku a/nebo přehlásky."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:114
msgid "In case you need a more exact search, you can turn it off:"
msgstr "Pokud potřebujete přesnější vyhledávání, můžete ji vypnout:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_asciifolding', false)\"\n"
msgstr "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_asciifolding', false)\"\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSL verification"
msgstr "Ověření SSL"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:122
msgid ""
"You can disable SSL verification, which is not recommended. Default is "
"`true`."
msgstr ""
"Ověření SSL můžete vypnout, což se nedoporučuje. Výchozí hodnota je `true`."

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_ssl_verify', false)\"\n"
msgstr "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_ssl_verify', false)\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:130
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to use custom certificates, you can find information about how to use\n"
"them in Zammad's admin settings\n"
"(_Settings > Security > SSL Certificates_).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pokud chcete používat vlastní certifikáty, informace o jejich použití\n"
"najdete v administraci Zammadu\n"
"(_Nastavení > Zabezpečení > SSL certifikáty_).\n"

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:133
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Troubleshooting unsuccessful or issue not described?\n"
"\n"
"If you can't solve your issue using the provided troubleshooting steps\n"
"or can't find your particular issue described here, feel free to\n"
"[ask the community](https://community.zammad.org){target=_blank} for technical\n"
"assistance.\n"
msgstr ""
"Řešení potíží nepomohlo nebo váš problém není popsán?\n"
"\n"
"Pokud se vám problém nepodaří vyřešit uvedenými kroky\n"
"nebo zde svůj konkrétní problém nenajdete, klidně\n"
"[se zeptejte komunity](https://community.zammad.org){target=_blank} a požádejte o technickou\n"
"pomoc.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data missing from the web-UI / search data missing or incomplete"
msgstr "Chybějící data ve webovém rozhraní / chybějící nebo neúplná data vyhledávání"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:148
msgid ""
"A commonly reported issue is data missing from the Web-UI. This could be "
"tickets, articles, users or anything else [indexed by Elasticsearch](/en/"
"reference/es-indexed-attributes)  and can be caused by missing or incomplete "
"indexes."
msgstr ""
"Často hlášeným problémem jsou chybějící data ve webovém rozhraní. Může jít o "
"tikety, články, uživatele nebo cokoli jiného, co [indexuje Elasticsearch](/"
"cs/reference/es-indexed-attributes), a příčinou mohou být chybějící nebo "
"neúplné indexy."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:152
msgid ""
"If you are experiencing this issue and installed Elasticsearch according to "
"our [installation guide](/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch), please follow "
"these steps to make sure Elasticsearch is working correctly."
msgstr ""
"Pokud tento problém máte a Elasticsearch jste nainstalovali podle našeho "
"[instalačního návodu](/cs/tutorials/install-elasticsearch), ověřte prosím "
"podle těchto kroků, že Elasticsearch funguje správně."

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:153
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Verify Elasticsearch is running"
msgstr "Krok 1: Ověřte, že Elasticsearch běží"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo systemctl status elasticsearch\n"
msgstr "sudo systemctl status elasticsearch\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:161
msgid ""
"This should output something like the following, make sure it says `Active: "
"active (running)`:"
msgstr ""
"Výstup by měl vypadat přibližně takto; ujistěte se, že obsahuje `Active: "
"active (running)`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"● elasticsearch.service - Elasticsearch\n"
"   Loaded: loaded (/lib/systemd/system/elasticsearch.service; enabled; vendor preset: enabled)\n"
"   Active: active (running) since Tue 2021-07-20 09:38:21 UTC; 1h 4min ago\n"
"   Docs: https://www.elastic.co\n"
"   Main PID: 1790 (java)\n"
msgstr ""
"● elasticsearch.service - Elasticsearch\n"
"   Loaded: loaded (/lib/systemd/system/elasticsearch.service; enabled; vendor preset: enabled)\n"
"   Active: active (running) since Tue 2021-07-20 09:38:21 UTC; 1h 4min ago\n"
"   Docs: https://www.elastic.co\n"
"   Main PID: 1790 (java)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:171
msgid "Otherwise, try restarting it and check again:"
msgstr "Jinak ho zkuste restartovat a zkontrolujte znovu:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo systemctl restart elasticsearch\n"
msgstr "sudo systemctl restart elasticsearch\n"

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:176
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If this fails, your Elasticsearch installation is probably broken.\n"
"Try completely purging and reinstalling Elasticsearch according to\n"
"our [installation guide](/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pokud to selže, vaše instalace Elasticsearch je pravděpodobně poškozená.\n"
"Zkuste Elasticsearch úplně odstranit a znovu nainstalovat podle\n"
"našeho [instalačního návodu](/cs/tutorials/install-elasticsearch).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Verify Zammad can access Elasticsearch and rebuild the indexes"
msgstr "Krok 2: Ověřte, že Zammad má přístup k Elasticsearch, a znovu sestavte indexy"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:186
msgid ""
"Force Zammad to drop and rebuild the Elasticsearch indexes, optionally with "
"a specified number of CPU cores to use for re-indexing (example `[8]`):"
msgstr ""
"Vynuťte, aby Zammad smazal a znovu sestavil indexy Elasticsearch, volitelně "
"s určeným počtem jader CPU pro přeindexování (příklad `[8]`):"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:192
msgid "This should start rebuilding the indexes and output its progress:"
msgstr "Tím by se mělo spustit nové sestavení indexů a vypisovat jeho průběh:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:193
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dropping indexes... done.\n"
"Deleting pipeline... done.\n"
"Creating indexes... done.\n"
"Creating pipeline... done.\n"
"Reloading data...\n"
"   - Chat::Session...\n"
"      done in 0 seconds.\n"
"   - Cti::Log...\n"
"      done in 0 seconds.\n"
"\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""
"Dropping indexes... done.\n"
"Deleting pipeline... done.\n"
"Creating indexes... done.\n"
"Creating pipeline... done.\n"
"Reloading data...\n"
"   - Chat::Session...\n"
"      done in 0 seconds.\n"
"   - Cti::Log...\n"
"      done in 0 seconds.\n"
"\n"
"[...]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:210
msgid ""
"Depending on the system performance and amount of data, this can take a "
"while to complete. Please let this task finish completely and wait until it "
"drops you back to the console."
msgstr ""
"V závislosti na výkonu systému a množství dat to může chvíli trvat. Nechte "
"prosím úlohu úplně doběhnout a počkejte, až vás vrátí do konzole."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:215
msgid ""
"If this fails or throws an error, there might be something else wrong with "
"your installation. Make sure you followed the complete Elasticsearch set up "
"and integration procedure according to our [installation guide](/en/"
"tutorials/install-elasticsearch)."
msgstr ""
"Pokud to selže nebo vyhodí chybu, může být s vaší instalací něco jiného v "
"nepořádku. Ujistěte se, že jste prošli celým postupem instalace a integrace "
"Elasticsearch podle našeho [instalačního návodu](/cs/tutorials/install-"
"elasticsearch)."

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:216
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In many situations where you're not successful with above steps, you\n"
"may want to check Elasticsearch's log file:\n"
"`/var/log/elasticsearch/elasticsearch.log`.\n"
msgstr ""
"V mnoha situacích, kdy výše uvedené kroky nepomohou, se\n"
"vyplatí zkontrolovat soubor protokolu Elasticsearch:\n"
"`/var/log/elasticsearch/elasticsearch.log`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:223
msgid ""
"After completing these steps, you should have verified your Elasticsearch "
"installation is running and rebuilt the indexes."
msgstr ""
"Po dokončení těchto kroků byste měli mít ověřeno, že vaše instalace "
"Elasticsearch běží, a indexy znovu sestavené."

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-css.md:1 src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-css.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom knowledge base CSS"
msgstr "Vlastní CSS znalostní báze"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-css.md:10
msgid ""
"You can apply visual changes to your public knowledge base via custom CSS.  "
"To do so, follow these steps:"
msgstr ""
"Vzhled veřejné znalostní báze můžete upravit pomocí vlastního CSS. "
"Postupujte takto:"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-css.md:20
msgid ""
"Add your CSS file(s) inside the directory `app/assets/stylesheets/"
"custom_knowledge_base_public` of your Zammad installation. You can use one "
"or more files and choose any name, as long as they have a `.css` extension."
msgstr ""
"Přidejte své CSS soubory do adresáře `app/assets/stylesheets/"
"custom_knowledge_base_public` vaší instalace Zammadu. Můžete použít jeden či "
"více souborů s libovolným názvem, pokud mají příponu `.css`."

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-css.md:20
msgid ""
"Precompile the assets by using the command `rake assets:precompile` (depends "
"on your installation method, see the [Rails commands](/en/reference/rails-"
"commands) reference)."
msgstr ""
"Předkompilujte assety příkazem `rake assets:precompile` (záleží na způsobu "
"instalace, viz reference [Příkazy Rails](/cs/reference/rails-commands))."

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-css.md:20
msgid "Restart Zammad."
msgstr "Restartujte Zammad."

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-css.md:20
msgid ""
"Access your published knowledge base. Please note: the visual changes only "
"affect the published version and not the edit screen."
msgstr ""
"Otevřete publikovanou znalostní bázi. Upozornění: vizuální změny se projeví "
"jen v publikované verzi, ne na obrazovce úprav."

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:1 src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom knowledge base URL"
msgstr "Vlastní URL znalostní báze"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:11
msgid ""
"If you want to publish Zammad's knowledge base under a different URL than "
"the default one, you can follow our configuration example using [NPM (Nginx "
"Proxy Manager)](https://nginxproxymanager.com/){target=_blank} below."
msgstr ""
"Pokud chcete znalostní bázi Zammadu publikovat pod jinou URL, než je "
"výchozí, můžete postupovat podle našeho příkladu konfigurace s [NPM (Nginx "
"Proxy Manager)](https://nginxproxymanager.com/){target=_blank} níže."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure Zammad"
msgstr "Konfigurace Zammadu"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:19
msgid ""
"Go to **Knowledge Base** in Zammad's admin settings and select the **Custom "
"URL** tab."
msgstr ""
"V administraci Zammadu přejděte do sekce **Znalostní báze** a vyberte kartu "
"**Vlastní URL**."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:19
msgid ""
"Add the URL you want to publish your knowledge base under and click the "
"`Submit` button."
msgstr ""
"Zadejte URL, pod kterou chcete znalostní bázi publikovat, a klikněte na "
"tlačítko `Odeslat`."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:19
msgid ""
"Click on the `Web Server Configuration` button to get the configuration for "
"your NPM. You can already copy the snippet or just leave it open; it is "
"needed for the NPM configuration."
msgstr ""
"Kliknutím na tlačítko `Konfigurace webového serveru` získáte konfiguraci pro "
"NPM. Úryvek si můžete rovnou zkopírovat, nebo ho nechat otevřený; budete ho "
"potřebovat při konfiguraci NPM."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure NPM"
msgstr "Konfigurace NPM"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:23
msgid "In NPM, add a new proxy host with the following parameters:"
msgstr "V NPM přidejte nového proxy hostitele s následujícími parametry:"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Details tab"
msgstr "Karta Details"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:29
msgid ""
"**Domain Names**: the domain under which you want to publish your knowledge "
"base"
msgstr "**Domain Names**: doména, pod kterou chcete znalostní bázi publikovat"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:29
msgid "**Forwarded Hostname / IP**: the host/IP of your Zammad instance"
msgstr "**Forwarded Hostname / IP**: hostitel/IP vaší instance Zammadu"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:29
msgid ""
"**Forward Port**: the port of your Zammad (by default `8080` in Portainer "
"deployment)"
msgstr ""
"**Forward Port**: port vašeho Zammadu (ve výchozím nastavení `8080` při "
"nasazení přes Portainer)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:31
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows NPM configuration dialog with details tab](/screenshots/"
"tutorials/custom-kb-url/npm-details-tab.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Snímek obrazovky zobrazující konfigurační dialog NPM s kartou Details](/"
"screenshots/tutorials/custom-kb-url/npm-details-tab.png)"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom location tab"
msgstr "Karta Custom location"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:40
msgid "**Define location**: `/`"
msgstr "**Define location**: `/`"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:40
msgid "**Forward Hostname / IP**: same as above"
msgstr "**Forward Hostname / IP**: stejné jako výše"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:40
msgid "**Forward Port**: same as above"
msgstr "**Forward Port**: stejný jako výše"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:40
msgid ""
"Click on the cogwheel to open the custom location configuration text field "
"and paste `proxy_set_header X-ORIGINAL-URL $request_uri;` (the lower part of "
"Zammad's snippet)"
msgstr ""
"Kliknutím na ozubené kolečko otevřete textové pole pro konfiguraci vlastního "
"umístění a vložte `proxy_set_header X-ORIGINAL-URL $request_uri;` (spodní "
"část úryvku ze Zammadu)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:42
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows NPM configuration dialog with custom locations tab](/"
"screenshots/tutorials/custom-kb-url/npm-custom-locations-tab.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Snímek obrazovky zobrazující konfigurační dialog NPM s kartou Custom "
"locations](/screenshots/tutorials/custom-kb-url/npm-custom-locations-tab.png)"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced tab"
msgstr "Karta Advanced"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Custom Nginx Configuration**: add the upper part of Zammad's snippet,\n"
"which should be similar to the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Custom Nginx Configuration**: přidejte horní část úryvku ze Zammadu,\n"
"která by měla vypadat podobně jako tato:\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Add following lines to \"server\" directive\n"
"if ($host = help.your.domain ) {\n"
"  rewrite ^/(api|assets)/(.*)$ /$1/$2 last;\n"
"  rewrite ^(.*)$ /help$1 last;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"# Add following lines to \"server\" directive\n"
"if ($host = help.your.domain ) {\n"
"  rewrite ^/(api|assets)/(.*)$ /$1/$2 last;\n"
"  rewrite ^(.*)$ /help$1 last;\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:57
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows NPM configuration dialog with advanced tab](/screenshots/"
"tutorials/custom-kb-url/npm-advanced-tab.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Snímek obrazovky zobrazující konfigurační dialog NPM s kartou Advanced](/"
"screenshots/tutorials/custom-kb-url/npm-advanced-tab.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/custom-kb-url.md:59
msgid ""
"After following these steps, your knowledge base should be published under a "
"custom URL. You can test it by clicking the preview button in your knowledge "
"base."
msgstr ""
"Po provedení těchto kroků by vaše znalostní báze měla být publikována pod "
"vlastní URL. Můžete to vyzkoušet kliknutím na tlačítko náhledu ve znalostní "
"bázi."

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Docker file handling examples"
msgstr "Příklady práce se soubory v Dockeru"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:10
msgid ""
"If you're not sure how to handle the backup files and how to create the "
"`restore` directory in the Docker volume, you can find some examples below."
msgstr ""
"Pokud si nejste jisti, jak zacházet se soubory zálohy a jak vytvořit adresář "
"`restore` v Docker volume, najdete níže několik příkladů."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restore inside the same stack"
msgstr "Obnova v rámci stejného stacku"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Requires:** console access to the zammad-backup container.\n"
msgstr "**Vyžaduje:** přístup ke konzoli kontejneru zammad-backup.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:18
msgid ""
"If you want to restore a backup from the same stack, you just have to create "
"the directory and copy/move the files into it. The following example starts "
"the **zammad-backup** container and copies _all_ .gz files from the backup "
"directory into the restore directory:"
msgstr ""
"Pokud chcete obnovit zálohu ze stejného stacku, stačí vytvořit adresář a "
"zkopírovat/přesunout do něj soubory. Následující příklad spustí kontejner "
"**zammad-backup** a zkopíruje _všechny_ soubory .gz z adresáře záloh do "
"adresáře obnovy:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker compose run --rm zammad-backup bash -c \"mkdir /var/tmp/zammad/restore; cp /var/tmp/zammad/*.gz /var/tmp/zammad/restore -v\"\n"
msgstr "docker compose run --rm zammad-backup bash -c \"mkdir /var/tmp/zammad/restore; cp /var/tmp/zammad/*.gz /var/tmp/zammad/restore -v\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:24
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:47
msgid "Now start the stack to execute the restore process."
msgstr "Nyní spusťte stack, čímž se provede obnova."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restore from another installation"
msgstr "Obnova z jiné instalace"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Requires:** console access to the host system and the zammad-backup container.\n"
msgstr "**Vyžaduje:** přístup ke konzoli hostitelského systému a kontejneru zammad-backup.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:31
msgid ""
"To **obtain** your backup files from another Docker Compose deployment, one "
"way is to copy it to the host system with `docker compose cp`:"
msgstr ""
"Chcete-li **získat** soubory zálohy z jiného nasazení Docker Compose, můžete "
"je například zkopírovat do hostitelského systému pomocí `docker compose cp`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker compose cp zammad-backup:/var/tmp/zammad/ /path/to/your/host/directory/\n"
msgstr "docker compose cp zammad-backup:/var/tmp/zammad/ /path/to/your/host/directory/\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:38
msgid ""
"In case you are searching for your backup files from a package installation, "
"have a look at the [Backup & Restore (Package)](/en/tutorials/backup-"
"restore) section. You don't need a full dump for restoring your backup."
msgstr ""
"Pokud hledáte soubory zálohy z balíčkové instalace, podívejte se do části "
"[Zálohování a obnova (balíček)](/cs/tutorials/backup-restore). K obnovení "
"zálohy nepotřebujete úplný výpis."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:41
msgid ""
"To **restore** the backup, place your files in a folder called `restore` on "
"the host system. This folder is mounted temporarily to `/restore` in the "
"backup container. The directory then gets copied to the actual directory:"
msgstr ""
"Chcete-li zálohu **obnovit**, umístěte soubory do složky `restore` v "
"hostitelském systému. Tato složka se dočasně připojí do `/restore` v "
"kontejneru zálohy. Adresář se pak zkopíruje do skutečného adresáře:"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker compose run --rm -v /path/to/your/host/directory:/restore zammad-backup bash -c \"cp -rv /restore /var/tmp/zammad/\"\n"
msgstr "docker compose run --rm -v /path/to/your/host/directory:/restore zammad-backup bash -c \"cp -rv /restore /var/tmp/zammad/\"\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a web GUI"
msgstr "Použití webového GUI"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Requires:** console access to the host system or Portainer access with the permission to deploy a container.\n"
msgstr "**Vyžaduje:** přístup ke konzoli hostitelského systému nebo přístup do Portaineru s oprávněním nasadit kontejner.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:53
msgid ""
"This can be useful if you use Portainer to deploy Zammad and have limited "
"access to the host system."
msgstr ""
"To se může hodit, pokud Zammad nasazujete přes Portainer a máte omezený "
"přístup k hostitelskému systému."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:57
msgid ""
"Our example uses the tool [filebrowser](https://filebrowser.org/)"
"{target=_blank}, but any similar tool should work too. If you'd like to use "
"such a tool permanently, make sure to provide additional volumes for "
"persistence (e.g. for their database)."
msgstr ""
"Náš příklad používá nástroj [filebrowser](https://filebrowser.org/)"
"{target=_blank}, ale fungovat by měl i jakýkoli podobný nástroj. Pokud "
"chcete takový nástroj používat trvale, zajistěte pro persistenci další "
"volumes (např. pro jeho databázi)."

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"The steps below cover the restore process by uploading files. To get your backup files in the same way from another\n"
"stack, you can follow steps 1-4 below and simply map the **zammad-backup** volume of your _old_ stack. Then you can\n"
"download the files, stop and remove the filebrowser container and redeploy it, following the steps below.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Kroky níže popisují obnovu nahráním souborů. Chcete-li stejným způsobem získat soubory zálohy z jiného\n"
"stacku, proveďte kroky 1–4 níže a jednoduše namapujte volume **zammad-backup** vašeho _starého_ stacku. Pak můžete\n"
"soubory stáhnout, kontejner filebrowser zastavit, odstranit a znovu nasadit podle kroků níže.\n"
"\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:67
msgid "Deploy filebrowser"
msgstr "Nasaďte filebrowser"

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"   === Via console\n"
"\n"
"   Deploy the container and provide the volume of **zammad-backup** and\n"
"   a port under which you want to access the web UI:\n"
"\n"
"   ``` sh\n"
"   docker run -v zammad-docker-compose_zammad-backup:/srv -p 8089:80 filebrowser/filebrowser\n"
"   ```\n"
"\n"
"   === Via Portainer\n"
"\n"
"   In your Portainer web UI, go to **Containers** in the left menu and\n"
"   click the `Add container` button.\n"
"\n"
"   Add the following information:\n"
"\n"
"   - Name: enter a name which is not already in use.\n"
"   - Image: `filebrowser/filebrowser`\n"
"   - Map additional port: choose a port and map it to port `80` in the container.\n"
"   - Advanced container settings:\n"
"     - Switch to **Volumes** and click the `map additional volume` button.\n"
"     - Enter `/srv` in the container section and select the volume containing `zammad-backup`\n"
"   - Finally, click on **Deploy the container**.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"   === Přes konzoli\n"
"\n"
"   Nasaďte kontejner, předejte mu volume **zammad-backup** a\n"
"   port, na kterém chcete webové rozhraní otevřít:\n"
"\n"
"   ``` sh\n"
"   docker run -v zammad-docker-compose_zammad-backup:/srv -p 8089:80 filebrowser/filebrowser\n"
"   ```\n"
"\n"
"   === Přes Portainer\n"
"\n"
"   Ve webovém rozhraní Portaineru přejděte v levém menu do **Containers** a\n"
"   klikněte na tlačítko `Add container`.\n"
"\n"
"   Zadejte následující informace:\n"
"\n"
"   - Name: zadejte název, který ještě není použitý.\n"
"   - Image: `filebrowser/filebrowser`\n"
"   - Map additional port: zvolte port a namapujte ho na port `80` v kontejneru.\n"
"   - Advanced container settings:\n"
"     - Přepněte na **Volumes** a klikněte na tlačítko `map additional volume`.\n"
"     - V části container zadejte `/srv` a vyberte volume obsahující `zammad-backup`\n"
"   - Nakonec klikněte na **Deploy the container**.\n"
"\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:102
msgid ""
"After the container is started, go to the web interface by using the IP "
"address and the port you defined."
msgstr ""
"Po spuštění kontejneru otevřete webové rozhraní pomocí IP adresy a portu, "
"který jste zvolili."

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:102
msgid "Log in with the default credentials `admin` / `admin`."
msgstr "Přihlaste se výchozími přihlašovacími údaji `admin` / `admin`."

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:102
msgid "You should now see at least 2 .gz files including a timestamp."
msgstr "Nyní byste měli vidět alespoň 2 soubory .gz s časovým razítkem."

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:102
msgid ""
"Create a `New folder` by using the button on the left side. Name it "
"**restore**."
msgstr ""
"Tlačítkem na levé straně vytvořte složku (`New folder`). Pojmenujte ji "
"**restore**."

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:102
msgid ""
"Enter this folder and upload your backup files (on the top right corner with "
"the up arrow). If the upload fails, it might be required to change the "
"permissions of the files (e.g. readable for everyone)."
msgstr ""
"Otevřete tuto složku a nahrajte soubory zálohy (v pravém horním rohu pomocí "
"šipky nahoru). Pokud nahrávání selže, může být nutné změnit oprávnění "
"souborů (např. čitelné pro všechny)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling.md:104
msgid ""
"Now start the stack to execute the restore process. After that, you can "
"safely delete the renamed folder and stop the filebrowser."
msgstr ""
"Nyní spusťte stack, čímž se provede obnova. Poté můžete přejmenovanou složku "
"bezpečně smazat a filebrowser zastavit."

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Firewall & SELinux"
msgstr "Firewall a SELinux"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:10
msgid ""
"This is just a collection of snippets which might be useful for you. Feel "
"free to skip parts and/or adapt it to your needs."
msgstr ""
"Toto je jen sbírka úryvků, které se vám mohou hodit. Klidně části přeskočte "
"a/nebo je upravte podle svých potřeb."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "SELinux"
msgstr "SELinux"

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following commands only work on Ubuntu, Debian and CentOS. If you use a\n"
"different distribution, please have a look at their documentation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Následující příkazy fungují jen na Ubuntu, Debianu a CentOS. Pokud používáte\n"
"jinou distribuci, podívejte se prosím do její dokumentace.\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo chcon -Rv --type=httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr "sudo chcon -Rv --type=httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo setsebool httpd_can_network_connect on -P\n"
msgstr "sudo setsebool httpd_can_network_connect on -P\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo semanage fcontext -a -t httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr "sudo semanage fcontext -a -t httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo restorecon -Rv /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr "sudo restorecon -Rv /opt/zammad/public/\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo chmod -R a+r /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr "sudo chmod -R a+r /opt/zammad/public/\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "Firewall"
msgstr "Firewall"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:43
msgid ""
"Ensure to open ports `80` and `443` (TCP & UDP) beside of the ports you "
"need. Below you can find a few examples for different distributions. If you "
"are using a different distribution, please have a look at their "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Kromě portů, které potřebujete, nezapomeňte otevřít porty `80` a `443` (TCP "
"i UDP). Níže najdete několik příkladů pro různé distribuce. Pokud používáte "
"jinou distribuci, podívejte se prosím do její dokumentace."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:46
msgid ""
"Please note that the examples below only cover the distribution’s default "
"firewall. It may not cover your case."
msgstr ""
"Příklady níže pokrývají jen výchozí firewall dané distribuce. Váš případ "
"pokrýt nemusí."

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"===Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw allow 80\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw allow 443\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===Debian\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"===Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw allow 80\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw allow 443\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo ufw reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===Debian\n"
"\n"

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|info)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We’re covering `nftables` in this part - `iptables` is discouraged\n"
"starting from Debian 10 (Buster). Our example uses the `input` chain, yours\n"
"may be a different one!\n"
msgstr ""
"V této části se věnujeme `nftables` – `iptables` se od Debianu 10 (Buster)\n"
"nedoporučuje. Náš příklad používá řetězec `input`, váš\n"
"může být jiný!\n"

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"Add the following lines to `/etc/nftables.conf` or your specific rule file.\n"
"Ensure to add these lines to your input-chain.\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"The result can look like the following. Keep in mind that your environment\n"
"could require different / more rules.\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"table inet filter {\n"
"   chain input {\n"
"      type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;\n"
"      ct state established,related accept\n"
"      tcp dport ssh log accept\n"
"      tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"      udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain forward {\n"
"      type filter hook forward priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain output {\n"
"      type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"To load the rules, run:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl reload nftables\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===CentOS, RHEL, OpenSUSE, SLES\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=http --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=https --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Přidejte následující řádky do `/etc/nftables.conf` nebo do svého souboru s pravidly.\n"
"Nezapomeňte je přidat do svého vstupního řetězce (input chain).\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Výsledek může vypadat takto. Mějte na paměti, že vaše prostředí\n"
"může vyžadovat jiná či další pravidla.\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"table inet filter {\n"
"   chain input {\n"
"      type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;\n"
"      ct state established,related accept\n"
"      tcp dport ssh log accept\n"
"      tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"      udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain forward {\n"
"      type filter hook forward priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain output {\n"
"      type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Pravidla načtete spuštěním:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl reload nftables\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===CentOS, RHEL, OpenSUSE, SLES\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=http --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=https --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:1 src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "First steps in Zammad"
msgstr "První kroky v Zammadu"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:11
msgid ""
"Congratulations, it seems you successfully installed Zammad. To start with "
"your fresh installed Zammad, head over to the next section. Alternatively, "
"you have other options:"
msgstr ""
"Gratulujeme, zdá se, že jste Zammad úspěšně nainstalovali. Chcete-li s "
"čerstvě nainstalovaným Zammadem začít, pokračujte další částí. Případně máte "
"další možnosti:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:14
msgid ""
"[Migrate from another supported ticketing system](/en/tutorials/migrate)"
msgstr ""
"[Migrace z jiného podporovaného systému pro správu tiketů](/cs/tutorials/"
"migrate)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:14
msgid "[Restore Zammad from an existing backup](/en/tutorials/backup-restore)"
msgstr "[Obnova Zammadu z existující zálohy](/cs/tutorials/backup-restore)"

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Getting started wizard"
msgstr "Průvodce úvodním nastavením"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:19
msgid ""
"If you visit Zammad's web page the first time, you'll be greeted by its "
"Getting Started Wizard. It will guide you through the first most important "
"things."
msgstr ""
"Když poprvé otevřete webovou stránku Zammadu, přivítá vás průvodce úvodním "
"nastavením. Provede vás tím nejdůležitějším na začátku."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Create your first administrator account"
msgstr "Krok 1: Vytvořte první účet administrátora"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:24
msgid ""
"Fill in the required information in the dialog. Your email address and "
"password are important. These are your credentials to log in."
msgstr ""
"Vyplňte v dialogu požadované údaje. Důležitá je e-mailová adresa a heslo. "
"Jsou to vaše přihlašovací údaje."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:26
msgid "Zammad applies the following password policy by default:"
msgstr "Zammad ve výchozím nastavení uplatňuje tyto zásady pro hesla:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:30
msgid "10 characters or more"
msgstr "10 nebo více znaků"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:30
msgid "At least 2 UPPER and 2 lower characters"
msgstr "Alespoň 2 VELKÁ a 2 malá písmena"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:30
msgid "One or more digits"
msgstr "Jedna nebo více číslic"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Provide company information"
msgstr "Krok 2: Zadejte informace o firmě"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:36
msgid ""
"You can upload a custom logo of your company here. The instance address is "
"detected automatically and only requires adjustment in case it is detected "
"wrong. If you skip it, you can adjust these things later too."
msgstr ""
"Zde můžete nahrát vlastní logo své firmy. Adresa instance se zjistí "
"automaticky a upravit ji je potřeba jen v případě, že byla zjištěna chybně. "
"Pokud tento krok přeskočíte, můžete tyto věci upravit i později."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Email notification channel"
msgstr "Krok 3: Kanál pro e-mailová oznámení"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:40
msgid "By default, Zammad uses sendmail. This can be changed to SMTP here."
msgstr ""
"Ve výchozím nastavení Zammad používá sendmail. Zde to můžete změnit na SMTP."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Zammad uses `noreply@<your-fqdn>` as sender address by default. SMTP setups\n"
"might fail - you can skip this step with choosing sendmail and adjust it later!\n"
msgstr ""
"Zammad ve výchozím nastavení používá jako adresu odesílatele `noreply@<your-fqdn>`. Nastavení SMTP\n"
"může selhat – tento krok můžete přeskočit volbou sendmail a upravit ho později!\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/first-steps.md:44
#, no-wrap
